{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/charts solid-js","lang":"sh"},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/solid'\n\nconst definition = createMemo(() =>\n  defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows()), { tooltip }),\n)\n\n;<Chart\n  definition={definition()}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue by month\"\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive props update the shared host without replacing its SVG. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"},{"type":"text","value":" target the outer host. The component renders the initial SVG during\nSolid SSR."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component creates one shared adapter controller, forwards reactive props\nfrom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createEffect"},{"type":"text","value":", mounts it in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMount"},{"type":"text","value":", and destroys it in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCleanup"},{"type":"text","value":".\nKeep stable definitions at module scope. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMemo"},{"type":"text","value":" for definitions that\ncapture reactive values."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ssr-and-hydration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR and hydration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid SSR emits the complete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-surface"},{"type":"text","value":", and\naccessible SVG. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" controls responsive server geometry.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createUniqueId()"},{"type":"text","value":" supplies the generated resource prefix. Keep server and\nbrowser definitions, formatters, and dimensions deterministic."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"presentation-and-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Presentation and rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style: JSX.CSSProperties"},{"type":"text","value":" apply to the outer host. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":"\napplies to the rendered chart surface. Custom outer styles are spread after\nadapter sizing. The component starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartCommonProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPresentationProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartProps"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-body-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip body composition"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={definition()}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  renderTooltipBody={(tooltip) => (\n    <div>\n      {tooltip.defaultBody}\n      <SeriesDetail points={tooltip.points} />\n      <Show when={tooltip.pinned}>\n        <button onClick={tooltip.dismiss}>Close</button>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the context through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of destructuring it so Solid tracks\nfocused points and pinned state. The shared host owns focus, placement,\nportaling, and dismissal; Solid owns the returned component lifecycle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/chart.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"../../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR and hydration"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\nand "},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"lifecycle","text":"Lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"ssr-and-hydration","text":"SSR and hydration","level":2},{"id":"presentation-and-rendering","text":"Presentation and rendering","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-body-composition","text":"Tooltip body composition","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts solid-js\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/solid'\n\nconst definition = createMemo(() =>\n  defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows()), { tooltip }),\n)\n\n;<Chart\n  definition={definition()}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue by month\"\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n/>\n```\n\nReactive props update the shared host without replacing its SVG. `class` and\n`style` target the outer host. The component renders the initial SVG during\nSolid SSR.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\nThe component creates one shared adapter controller, forwards reactive props\nfrom `createEffect`, mounts it in `onMount`, and destroys it in `onCleanup`.\nKeep stable definitions at module scope. Use `createMemo` for definitions that\ncapture reactive values.\n\n## SSR and hydration\n\nSolid SSR emits the complete `.ts-chart-host`, `.ts-chart-surface`, and\naccessible SVG. `initialWidth` controls responsive server geometry.\n`createUniqueId()` supplies the generated resource prefix. Keep server and\nbrowser definitions, formatters, and dimensions deterministic.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\n`class` and `style: JSX.CSSProperties` apply to the outer host. `className`\napplies to the rendered chart surface. Custom outer styles are spread after\nadapter sizing. The component starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n`canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `Chart`, `ChartCommonProps`, `ChartPresentationProps`, `ChartProps`,\n`ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`, `ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition()}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  renderTooltipBody={(tooltip) => (\n    <div>\n      {tooltip.defaultBody}\n      <SeriesDetail points={tooltip.points} />\n      <Show when={tooltip.pinned}>\n        <button onClick={tooltip.dismiss}>Close</button>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )}\n/>\n```\n\nRead the context through `tooltip` instead of destructuring it so Solid tracks\nfocused points and pinned state. The shared host owns focus, placement,\nportaling, and dismissal; Solid owns the returned component lifecycle.\n\nSee the [`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md), [SSR and hydration](../../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md),\nand [Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Solid Adapter\ndescription: Render and hydrate TanStack Charts with Solid.\n---\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts solid-js\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/solid'\n\nconst definition = createMemo(() =>\n  defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows()), { tooltip }),\n)\n\n;<Chart\n  definition={definition()}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue by month\"\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n/>\n```\n\nReactive props update the shared host without replacing its SVG. `class` and\n`style` target the outer host. The component renders the initial SVG during\nSolid SSR.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\nThe component creates one shared adapter controller, forwards reactive props\nfrom `createEffect`, mounts it in `onMount`, and destroys it in `onCleanup`.\nKeep stable definitions at module scope. Use `createMemo` for definitions that\ncapture reactive values.\n\n## SSR and hydration\n\nSolid SSR emits the complete `.ts-chart-host`, `.ts-chart-surface`, and\naccessible SVG. `initialWidth` controls responsive server geometry.\n`createUniqueId()` supplies the generated resource prefix. Keep server and\nbrowser definitions, formatters, and dimensions deterministic.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\n`class` and `style: JSX.CSSProperties` apply to the outer host. `className`\napplies to the rendered chart surface. Custom outer styles are spread after\nadapter sizing. The component starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n`canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `Chart`, `ChartCommonProps`, `ChartPresentationProps`, `ChartProps`,\n`ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`, `ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition()}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  renderTooltipBody={(tooltip) => (\n    <div>\n      {tooltip.defaultBody}\n      <SeriesDetail points={tooltip.points} />\n      <Show when={tooltip.pinned}>\n        <button onClick={tooltip.dismiss}>Close</button>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )}\n/>\n```\n\nRead the context through `tooltip` instead of destructuring it so Solid tracks\nfocused points and pinned state. The shared host owns focus, placement,\nportaling, and dismissal; Solid owns the returned component lifecycle.\n\nSee the [`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md), [SSR and hydration](../../guides/ssr-and-hydration.md),\nand [Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n"}
